==Introduction==

===Abstract===

[https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0352.mediawiki BIP-352 Silent Payments] give Bitcoin users a reusable static address whose on-chain footprints are unlinkable. [https://github.com/ElementsProject/ELIPs/blob/main/elip-0150.mediawiki Confidential Transactions (CT)] give Liquid users outputs whose asset and amount are hidden. These solve orthogonal privacy problems: CT conceals '''what''' moved; Silent Payments conceal '''who''' received it at the script level.

This ELIP defines their composition for the Liquid Network under protocol version&nbsp;0 (<code>spv0</code>). The BIP-352 ECDH spend path, input aggregation, partial tweaks, and label scheme are imported without modification. The Liquid-specific work is the '''CT envelope''': encoding each derived payment as a confidential P2WPKH output, deriving a per-output blinding key from the shared secret in a separate hash domain, and specifying wallet/indexer behaviour so receivers can scan, unblind, and spend without any out-of-band blinding-key exchange.

The document further specifies <code>lsp</code>/<code>tlsp</code> address encoding, the <code>elsp</code> descriptor, optional PSET metadata, a full-node receive path, and a tweak-server light-client path aligned with the anonymous profile of the [https://github.com/silent-payments/BIP0352-index-server-specification BIP-352 index server specification]. No consensus or relay changes are required.

