Prefix <code>LiquidSilentPayment</code> for co-signers that cannot re-derive outputs:

{| Suffix !! Value
|-
| <code>/sp_version</code> || <code>0x00</code>
|-
| <code>/sp_scan_pubkey</code> || 33 bytes
|-
| <code>/sp_spend_pubkey</code> || 33 bytes
|-
| <code>/sp_output_index</code> || <code>ser32(k)</code>
|-
| <code>/sp_label</code> || <code>ser32(m)</code>, omitted if none
|}

==Spending==

Controlled by one-off scalar <code>d_k</code> (+ label scalar), not a BIP-32 leaf.

'''Software signers''' MUST sign P2WPKH inputs given <code>d_k</code> or <code>(b_spend, t_k + label_scalar)</code> via standard ECDSA.

'''Hardware signers''' (Jade, Ledger) register fixed derivation paths and cannot apply per-UTXO additive tweaks in current protocols — out of scope for v0.

When spending a silent-payment UTXO alongside ordinary <code>ct(..., elwpkh(...))</code> coins, the PSET MUST include correct unblinded input data for each input; silent-payment inputs use <code>d_k</code> as the signing key for that input's P2WPKH script.

==Recovery==

From seed only: derive <code>b_scan</code>, <code>b_spend</code> via BIP-32 paths; rescan from <code>birth_height</code> (or wallet creation height).

* '''UTXO set recovery:''' scan eligible transactions with unspent P2WPKH outputs only.
* '''Full history:''' scan all eligible transactions.
* '''Labels:''' persist label set in backup; on seed-only recovery always scan <code>m = 0</code>; if label usage is unknown, precompute and check a large label range (BIP-352 recommends up to 100k) or restore label metadata from backup.

Matched-payment ledger + seed is strictly stronger than seed alone.

