==Design decisions==

{| Decision !! Choice !! Rejected !! Why
|-
| HRP || <code>lsp</code>/<code>tlsp</code> || <code>lq</code>/<code>tlq</code> || Existing CT HRP collision
|-
| Output (v0) || Confidential P2WPKH || P2TR || Matches deployed Liquid wallets; Taproot in v1
|-
| Blinding || <code>bk_k</code> from <code>S</code> || Script-derived; fixed address blinding || Scan-time discovery requires script-independent blinding
|-
| Indexer filters || Direct script match || Mandatory BIP-158 || Liquid scripts are public
|-
| Receive paths || Full node + tweak server || Server only || Privacy, regtest, CI
|}

==Backwards compatibility==

Opt-in. No impact on existing CT wallets or consensus. On-chain, a silent-payment UTXO is a normal confidential P2WPKH output — validators need no changes. Only wallets implementing this ELIP can detect and spend via <code>d_k</code>.

==Security considerations==

* '''Scan key exposure''' — detection without spend authority; export only to trusted scan processes.
* '''Indexer metadata''' — height polling reveals activity patterns; jitter and batch requests.
* '''<code>K_max</code>''' — limits worst-case scan to <code>O(N · K_max)</code> per block (BIP-352).
* '''Input ownership''' — aggregated inputs SHOULD belong to one sender.
* '''CT composition''' — independent review recommended before Final.

==Reference implementation==

[https://github.com/Blockstream/lwk LWK] is the intended integration target: new <code>lwk_sp</code> crate (BIP-352 core + CT envelope), tweak-server client in <code>lwk_wollet::clients</code>, tweaked-key signing in <code>lwk_signer</code>, silent-payment UTXO store separate from descriptor-based <code>Wollet</code> cache. SHOULD ship with this ELIP before Final.

